From 56fb2ac979b3675ce68815efcc77a0bf35f42981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bojie Li <bojieli@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:35:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QC xhead3: tid strap and a_pr width contract (literal row
 constants, no constant flops); HELD pending lec.py e6d2675979 rerun

Routed LEC NEQ on slw_hc2 cl6bcaba89 / cl16607c7a (b_emin row 11 bits 13..15): the gate removed tid/r_q
flops that are row constants only through tid() arithmetic. Only the cid bits are registered now; row
bits and zero top bits are literals; r_q and a_pr are plain vectors at reachable width. Function
unchanged for every input, 0 added cycles. Bench: self lockstep vs f41d943961 on 64 cids incl. a_pr /
b_emin state PASS, legacy lockstep PASS, mutants tidk/retag/rot/poolw/fwd FAIL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
